Played it for so long I don't know who I am anymore. I do know that Fish can roll, however.
The thing is, this game is all about making mistakes and learning from them. Paying attention to the words in between levels is pretty useful as well. As my first rougelike, bullet hell game it's incredibly addicting and now I have super-high expectations for similar games ;w;
It's great for someone who has a lot of patience and able to adapt to a 90 degree learning curve. Reaching the Throne is incredibly satisfying and I can feel this game is going to become really great later on.

Not the best season of the game for a few reasons I will list:
- reduced length of chapters compared to season 1;
- protagonist is meh;
- convoluted story/gameplay even more than season 1 (probably a result of rushed development).
All in all I can still recommend it especially if you played season 1, even more if its on sale.
